Requirements: 34   with obligations: 33   deliberately none: 1

[task-01] Obligation derivation issues one model call for the whole requirement
    registry. At scale that call sheds work: an observed run over roughly 36
    requirements, at about 2.5k input tokens, produced no obligation for 9 of them. That
    is DR-164's judgments-per-request failure, one stage earlier than the mapping stage
    where it was first found and fixed.
    -> obligation-ceil-calls-per-size  [functional/explicit]   (also serves constraint-10, completion-02)
       Produce `ceil(N / size)` derivation calls for a task file with `N` requirements.
    -> obligation-partition-derivation-by-batch  [functional/explicit]   (also serves task-03, constraint-01, constraint-03)
       Partition obligation derivation by requirement batch using the existing
       partitioning flow, and make the batch size configurable from the command line as
       `--decompose-batch-size`.

[task-02] The same call also links. It may attach a requirement to an obligation derived
    from a different requirement, and that linking fails in both directions on one task
    file under the same code, model and seed: seven scope exclusions declined with
    reasons that stated the obligation, then all five over-merged onto another
    requirement's obligation, with two Constraints absorbed into an obligation stating
    neither. Absorbed content is gone, and the run still reports every requirement as
    carrying a disposition, because that count reports dispositions rather than
    coverage.
    -> obligation-no-linking-in-derivation  [functional/explicit]   (also serves task-03, constraint-06)
       Keep derivation free of cross-requirement linking so that a call may split one
       requirement into several obligations or decline it with `no_obligation`, while
       each obligation remains associated only with the requirement that produced it.
    -> obligation-unique-obligation-per-requirement  [invariant/explicit]   (also serves constraint-07)
       Ensure that within one derivation response each obligation id appears in exactly
       one requirement's disposition.
    -> obligation-unusable-on-shared-obligation  [error_handling/explicit]   (also serves constraint-08, completion-05)
       Record a response that names one obligation from two requirements through
       `UnusableAnswerLog`, and leave both affected requirements undisposed.

[task-03] Partition obligation derivation by requirement batch, and stop derivation from
    linking at all.
    -> obligation-partition-derivation-by-batch  [functional/explicit]   (also serves task-01, constraint-01, constraint-03)
       Partition obligation derivation by requirement batch using the existing
       partitioning flow, and make the batch size configurable from the command line as
       `--decompose-batch-size`.
    -> obligation-no-linking-in-derivation  [functional/explicit]   (also serves task-02, constraint-06)
       Keep derivation free of cross-requirement linking so that a call may split one
       requirement into several obligations or decline it with `no_obligation`, while
       each obligation remains associated only with the requirement that produced it.

[constraint-01] Obligation derivation is partitioned by requirement batch, through the
    existing `partition.py` rather than a second partitioning mechanism.
    -> obligation-partition-derivation-by-batch  [functional/explicit]   (also serves task-01, task-03, constraint-03)
       Partition obligation derivation by requirement batch using the existing
       partitioning flow, and make the batch size configurable from the command line as
       `--decompose-batch-size`.

[constraint-02] The whole task file appears in every derivation prompt. The batch scopes
    which requirements a call must answer for; it does not scope what the call may read.
    -> obligation-whole-task-file-in-prompt  [invariant/explicit]
       Include the whole task file in every derivation prompt while using the batch only
       to determine which requirements the call must answer for.

[constraint-03] `RunConfig.decompose_batch_size` exists and is settable from the command
    line as `--decompose-batch-size`.
    -> obligation-partition-derivation-by-batch  [functional/explicit]   (also serves task-01, task-03, constraint-01)
       Partition obligation derivation by requirement batch using the existing
       partitioning flow, and make the batch size configurable from the command line as
       `--decompose-batch-size`.

[constraint-04] The batch size is treated as a determinism control exactly as
    `mapping_batch_size` is: only the size enters the hashed request, and the batch
    index and batch count never do.
    -> obligation-batch-size-determinism-control  [invariant/explicit]   (also serves completion-06)
       Treat decompose batch size as the determinism control for derivation requests so
       that only the size contributes to the hashed request, while batch index and batch
       count do not.

[constraint-05] A batch answers only for the requirements it was supplied. A returned
    requirement id that was not supplied to that call is recorded through
    `UnusableAnswerLog` rather than silently filtered.
    -> obligation-supplied-requirements-only  [error_handling/explicit]   (also serves completion-04)
       Record any returned requirement id that was not supplied to the derivation call
       through `UnusableAnswerLog`.

[constraint-06] Obligation derivation performs no linking. A call may split one
    requirement into several obligations, or decline it with `no_obligation`, but it may
    not attach a requirement to an obligation derived from another requirement.
    -> obligation-no-linking-in-derivation  [functional/explicit]   (also serves task-02, task-03)
       Keep derivation free of cross-requirement linking so that a call may split one
       requirement into several obligations or decline it with `no_obligation`, while
       each obligation remains associated only with the requirement that produced it.

[constraint-07] Within one derivation response, each obligation id appears in exactly
    one requirement's disposition.
    -> obligation-unique-obligation-per-requirement  [invariant/explicit]   (also serves task-02)
       Ensure that within one derivation response each obligation id appears in exactly
       one requirement's disposition.

[constraint-08] A response naming one obligation from two requirements is recorded
    through `UnusableAnswerLog`, and neither affected requirement is treated as
    disposed.
    -> obligation-unusable-on-shared-obligation  [error_handling/explicit]   (also serves task-02, completion-05)
       Record a response that names one obligation from two requirements through
       `UnusableAnswerLog`, and leave both affected requirements undisposed.

[constraint-09] Merged results are ordered deterministically, so batch composition and
    merge order are pure functions of the input.
    -> obligation-deterministic-merge-order  [invariant/explicit]
       Keep merged results ordered deterministically so that batch composition and merge
       order are pure functions of the input.

[constraint-10] A task file with N requirements produces ceil(N / size) derivation
    calls.
    -> obligation-ceil-calls-per-size  [functional/explicit]   (also serves task-01, completion-02)
       Produce `ceil(N / size)` derivation calls for a task file with `N` requirements.

[constraint-11] Every requirement carries a disposition after the merge.
    -> obligation-every-requirement-disposed-after-merge  [functional/explicit]   (also serves completion-03)
       Ensure that every requirement carries a disposition after the merge.

[constraint-12] Changing the decompose batch size invalidates recorded transcripts.
    -> obligation-batch-size-invalidates-transcripts  [compatibility/explicit]
       Invalidate recorded transcripts when the decompose batch size changes.

[constraint-13] Two runs over byte-identical task text produce byte-identical review
    state.
    -> obligation-byte-identical-review-state  [regression/explicit]   (also serves completion-07)
       Produce byte-identical review state for two runs over byte-identical task text.

[constraint-14] `ReviewProvenance.request_partition_size` reports the size observed from
    the calls rather than the size read from configuration.
    -> obligation-request-partition-size-from-calls  [functional/explicit]   (also serves completion-08)
       Have `ReviewProvenance.request_partition_size` report the size observed from the
       calls rather than the size read from configuration.

[constraint-15] Typed schemas are pydantic models, as the rest of the repository defines
    them.
    -> obligation-pydantic-schemas  [compatibility/explicit]
       Represent typed schemas as pydantic models.

[constraint-16] Tests issue no live model calls.
    -> obligation-tests-no-live-model-calls  [docs_config/explicit]
       Keep tests free of live model calls.

[exclusion-01] De-duplicating obligations, and attaching a requirement to an obligation
    derived from another requirement, which is #144 and lands immediately after this
    change.
    -> obligation-no-dedup-pass-partitioning  [human_review/explicit]   (also serves exclusion-06)
       Preserve the open question about whether the de-duplication pass itself needs
       partitioning.
    -> obligation-no-linking-scope-exclusion  [regression/explicit]
       Preserve the scope exclusion that de-duplicating obligations and attaching a
       requirement to an obligation derived from another requirement is handled by the
       later change.

[exclusion-02] Scoring link precision, which is #211 and which measures #144's output
    rather than this pass.
    -> obligation-no-link-precision-scoring  [regression/explicit]
       Preserve the separation from link precision scoring work so this pass does not
       measure #144's output.

[exclusion-03] The wording of the decomposition prompt beyond what partitioning and the
    no-linking rule require, which is #205, #206 and #219.
    -> obligation-prompt-wording-scope  [docs_config/explicit]
       Preserve the prompt wording scope so that only partitioning and the no-linking
       rule constrain the decomposition prompt.

[exclusion-04] Whether an obligation needs test evidence at all, which is #148.
    -> obligation-no-test-evidence-policy-change  [regression/explicit]
       Preserve the existing policy boundary about whether an obligation needs test
       evidence at all.

[exclusion-05] Recovering the requirements a prior run dropped, or comparing obligation
    counts against recorded transcripts.
    -> obligation-no-recovery-or-count-comparison  [regression/explicit]
       Preserve the exclusion of recovering requirements from prior dropped runs and
       comparing obligation counts against recorded transcripts.

[exclusion-06] Whether the de-duplication pass itself needs partitioning, which is a
    question #144 answers.
    -> obligation-no-dedup-pass-partitioning  [human_review/explicit]   (also serves exclusion-01)
       Preserve the open question about whether the de-duplication pass itself needs
       partitioning.

